<title>USA: Santa Fe, N.M., $13 mln at 5.88 pct yld in 2021.</title>
<headline>Santa Fe, N.M., $13 mln at 5.88 pct yld in 2021.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southwest Securities Inc, Dallas, Texas, said Tuesday it priced a $13.2 million Santa Fe, N.M., Municipal Recreation complex subordinate net revenue subordinate lien gross receipts tax revenue bond issue, Series 1996C, with a top yield of 5.88 percent in 2021.</p>
<p>The bonds are AMBAC insured and rated Aaa by Moody's Investors Service and AAA by Standard &amp; Poor's Corp.</p>
<p>The bonds are dated 9/15/1996. The first coupon is 6/1/1997. The bonds are due 6/1.</p>
<p>The bonds are callable 6/1/2007 at 100.00.</p>
<p>A sinking fund begins for 2016 maturity in 2013.</p>
<p>A sinking fund begins for 2021 maturity in 2017.  </p>
